---
id: org.dxos.plugin.transcription
name: TranscriptionPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

A real-time voice-to-text transcription plugin for DXOS Composer.
Captures spoken audio from a microphone, converts it to timestamped text segments via the
Whisper speech-recognition service, and stores the results in an ECHO `Transcript` object
backed by a `Feed`.
The plugin also exposes skill-compatible operations that let AI assistants open and
summarize transcripts inside agent workflows.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`       |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`   |

## Types

```mdl
type TranscriptSegment
  fields:
    text: string              # transcribed text for this segment
    started: string           # ISO-8601 wall-clock timestamp of segment start
```

```mdl
type Message
  fields:
    id: string
    created: string           # ISO-8601 creation timestamp
    blocks: TranscriptSegment[]
    sender:
      identityDid?: string    # DID of the speaker, if known
```

```mdl
type Transcript
  fields:
    id: string
    feed: Ref<Feed>           # ECHO feed that stores Message objects
    started?: string          # ISO-8601 timestamp when recording started
```

```mdl
type WhisperWord
  fields:
    word: string
    start: number             # seconds from start of audio chunk
    end: number
```

```mdl
type WhisperSegment
  fields:
    text: string
    start: number
    end: number
    no_speech_prob: number    # probability of silence; used to filter noise
    words: WhisperWord[]
```

```mdl
type Settings
  fields:
    entityExtraction: boolean    # default: true — annotate transcript with references to known objects
```

## Components

```mdl
component Transcription
  desc: Read-only CodeMirror editor that renders transcript messages as Markdown with byline headings.
  props:
    transcript?: Transcript
    model: TranscriptModel<Message>
  slots:
    (none — self-contained editor viewport)
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
    │ [CodeMirror editor — read-only] │
    │  ## Speaker · HH:MM             │
    │  Transcribed text…              │
    │  …                              │
    └─────────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component Oracle
  desc: |
    Ambient display surface with an SVG graph canvas and a centered text overlay.
    Used to show the latest transcribed utterance alongside a live visualization.
  props:
    text?: string             # latest utterance to display
    delay?: number            # per-character reveal delay in ms (default 12)
  slots:
    canvas?: ReactNode        # replaces default SVG.Graph when provided
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
    │  [SVG canvas — absolutely fills]│
    │         [Oracle.Text]           │
    │   "latest utterance…"           │
    └─────────────────────────────────┘
```

```mdl
component TranscriptionArticle
  desc: Full-page article panel combining the Transcription editor with a start/stop recording toolbar action.
  props:
    subject: Transcript
    role: string
    attendableId?: string
  state:
    recording: boolean        # whether microphone capture is active
  actions:
    toggleRecording()
  layout: |
    ┌─────────────────────────────────┐
    │ [Toolbar]  [🎤 Start/Stop]      │
    ├─────────────────────────────────┤
    │ [Transcription editor]          │
    │  …                              │
    └─────────────────────────────────┘
```

## Operations

Pure operations — no side-effects.

```mdl
op openTranscript
  key: org.dxos.operation.transcription.open
  desc: Loads a Transcript from ECHO, reads all Messages from its Feed, and returns the full text content rendered with speaker bylines.
  input:
    transcript: Ref<Transcript>
  output: string
  errors:
    TranscriptNotFound: no Transcript object found for the given ref
    FeedNotFound: the Transcript's feed ref cannot be resolved
  requires: [Database, FeedService]
```

Effectful operations — produce output via AI or mutate persistent state.

```mdl
op createTranscript
  key: org.dxos.operation.transcription.create
  desc: Creates a new Feed and a Transcript object linked to it, then writes both into the current ECHO space.
  input:
    name?: string
    space: Space
  output: Transcript
  effects: [echo:write]
```

```mdl
op summarizeTranscript
  key: org.dxos.operation.transcription.summarize
  desc: Sends a transcript string and optional participant notes to an LLM and returns a Markdown summary with key points, verbatim quotes, and actionable tasks extracted from the conversation.
  input:
    transcript: string
    notes?: string
  output: string
  effects: [http]
  requires: [AiService]
  note: |
    Uses Claude Sonnet. Prompt instructs the model to bold speaker names,
    include verbatim quotes, and emit only tasks that are directly actionable
    and clearly assigned.
```

```mdl
op enrichMessage
  key: org.dxos.operation.transcription.enrichMessage
  desc: Extracts proper nouns from each transcript block of a Message using a small LLM, full-text-searches the space for matching objects, and rewrites the text with inline `[noun](dxn)` reference links.
  input:
    message: Message
  output:
    message: Message
  effects: [echo:read, ai:inference]
  requires: [AiService, Database]
  note: |
    Uses Claude Haiku. Falls back to the raw message if extraction fails (e.g. the AI
    service is unavailable). Gated by the entityExtraction setting.
```

```mdl
op normalizeSentences
  key: org.dxos.operation.transcription.normalizeSentence
  desc: Post-processes an array of raw transcript messages, merging word-level tokens into grammatically complete sentences.
  input:
    messages: Message[]
  output: Message[]
  note: pure transformation; no effects or service dependencies
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: Recording Lifecycle

  req F-1.1: User can start microphone capture from TranscriptionArticle toolbar.
  req F-1.2: User can stop microphone capture; final buffered chunks are flushed and transcribed.
  req F-1.3: TranscriptionManager restarts the Transcriber automatically when the audio track changes.
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Audio Chunking and Transcription

  req F-2.1:
    when: user is speaking and chunk count reaches transcribeAfterChunksAmount
    then: Transcriber schedules a deferred transcription task

  req F-2.2:
    when: transcription task runs
    then: buffered PCM chunks are merged into a WAV file and POSTed to the Whisper endpoint

  req F-2.3:
    when: Whisper response is received
    then: segments are filtered by no_speech_prob and aligned to absolute wall-clock timestamps

  req F-2.4:
    when: user is not speaking
    then: only prefixBufferChunksAmount most-recent chunks are retained; older chunks discarded
```

```mdl
feat F-3: Transcript Persistence

  req F-3.1:
    when: aligned segments are produced
    then: a Message object with the segments is appended to the Transcript's ECHO Feed

  req F-3.2:
    when: a messageEnricher is configured
    then: Message is passed through the enricher before being written to the Feed

  req F-3.3:
    when: a peer's ECHO space receives the Feed update
    then: TranscriptionArticle re-renders with the new messages
    tags: [collaborative]
```

```mdl
feat F-4: Transcript Display

  req F-4.1:
    when: a Transcript object is opened
    then: all Messages are rendered in the Transcription editor with speaker bylines and timestamps

  req F-4.2:
    when: new messages arrive during live recording
    then: the TranscriptModel is updated and the editor scrolls to show the latest content
```

```mdl
feat F-5: AI Summary

  req F-5.1:
    when: op:summarizeTranscript is invoked
    then: LLM returns a structured Markdown document with key points, quotes, and tasks

  req F-5.2:
    when: participant notes are provided
    then: notes are correlated with transcript content in the summary

  req F-5.3:
    when: no actionable tasks are found
    then: the tasks section is omitted from the summary
```

```mdl
feat F-6: Skill Integration

  req F-6.1: Skill exposes op:openTranscript and op:summarizeTranscript as AI tools.
  req F-6.2: An AI assistant can open a transcript by Ref and return formatted text to the user.
  req F-6.3: An AI assistant can invoke the summary operation and present the result as a message.
```

```mdl
feat F-7: On-device Streaming Transcription (Whistle story)

  req F-7.1:
    when: the user presses Record, or holds Space outside a text field
    then: the microphone streams into Whistle in a worker as one stream, re-decoded after every pass interval of new audio; nothing leaves the tab
  req F-7.2:
    when: two consecutive passes agree on a word
    then: the word is committed; the unconfirmed tail is shown in italics after the last paragraph
  req F-7.3: The pass interval is 1 s, as in Cactus's demo; Low latency makes it 200 ms, which commits sooner but agrees on half-heard words more often.
  req F-7.4:
    when: the audio holds 1.5 s of silence or more between two committed words, or the stream stops
    then: a new paragraph starts; silence is measured in the audio against the noise floor, not between the model's word times
  req F-7.5: Without a pause, a paragraph closes at the first sentence end after 30 words.
  req F-7.6: Keywords bias recognition from the next pass; the list is prefilled with DXOS terms.
  req F-7.7: The whole recording stays in the tab; each paragraph can be played back or saved as WAV, and so can the whole recording.
  req F-7.8: The engine and model download on first use only and are kept in Cache Storage; mounting the story downloads nothing.
  req F-7.9: After first use the microphone stays open, so push-to-talk does not clip the first word.
  req F-7.10:
    when: the audio holds no sound louder than -35 dBFS for 0.15 s
    then: no stream is opened and nothing is decoded, so Whistle cannot invent words in silence or room tone; the last 0.5 s before sound is kept so the first word is heard from its onset
```

```mdl
feat F-8: On-device Voice Home Assistant (Home story)

  req F-8.1:
    when: the user holds Space, or toggles Talk, and says a request such as "turn on the kitchen lights"
    then: Whistle transcribes it as it is spoken, and Needle 3, loaded into the same engine and worker, answers it against five home tools when the request ends
  req F-8.2: The tools are set_lights, set_thermostat, operate_door, set_blinds and play_music; each call changes a mock home drawn as a floor plan, and the rooms it touched are highlighted.
  req F-8.3:
    when: a request ends
    then: it is answered from the stream's committed words and its latest unconfirmed tail, before the stream's closing pass; audio after a pass that already heard 0.15 s of silence is not decoded again
  req F-8.4: Low latency (on by default) caps the answer at 32 tokens, which skips the model's reasoning line; a request that joins actions with "and", "then" or "also" keeps the 128-token budget so every call survives.
  req F-8.5:
    when: Hands-free is on and the microphone is open
    then: a request ends after 0.7 s of silence following speech (0.5 s in Low latency), found in the audio as it reaches the worker, and capture continues into the next request
  req F-8.10: Silence is handled in the worker, in audio time: passes pause once the stream has heard 0.15 s of silence, and a stream that hears nothing for 1 s is ended at the next silence, so each request's stream holds little more than the request.
  req F-8.6:
    when: the model withholds a call (suppressed_calls)
    then: it is offered as "Did you mean …?" and runs only when the user confirms it
  req F-8.7:
    when: no tool serves the request
    then: the log says so and nothing changes
  req F-8.8: Each command in the log shows its transcript, what changed, the calls, the time from the end of the request to the answer, and the model's time and confidence.
  req F-8.9: Call arguments are checked against the home before they apply; an argument outside the schema is an error in the log, never a change.
```

```mdl
feat F-9: Audio Tooling and Evals

  req F-9.1: The audio-view skill describes a recording's levels and speech/silence timeline as text, draws a labelled spectrogram, and replays it through the pinned Whistle engine in Node exactly as the story streams it.
  req F-9.2: Recordings with real voices are private fixtures in the encrypted test-fixtures bucket, never in git; the agents scope holds whistle-silence, whistle-one-two-three, whistle-echo-query-a and whistle-echo-query-b.
  req F-9.3:
    when: the manual Whistle evals run and a fixture is present
    then: each recording is replayed through the story's silence gate and its word error rate against the expected transcript, the words committed during silence and keyword recall are reported; whistle-silence must commit no words; a missing fixture skips its test, and CI does not run them
  req F-9.4: A compare script runs one recording through larger hosted models (OpenAI whisper-1 and gpt-4o-transcribe, Cloudflare Workers AI whisper-large-v3-turbo), skips a provider without credentials, and prints the transcripts side by side with word error rate against a reference. Anthropic's API takes no audio input, so it is not compared.
```

## Acceptance

```mdl
scenario T-1: Create transcript
  given: a DXOS space is available
  when: op:createTranscript is invoked
  then:
    - a new Feed is created in the space
    - a Transcript object linked to the Feed is created in the space
    - the returned Transcript.feed.target is not null
```

```mdl
scenario T-2: Record and persist segment
  given: a Transcript with a Feed, microphone capture active
  when: the user speaks and silence is detected
  then:
    - Whisper returns at least one segment
    - a Message is appended to the Feed
    - Message.blocks contains at least one TranscriptSegment with non-empty text
```

```mdl
scenario T-3: Deduplicate segments across chunk boundaries
  given: two consecutive transcription tasks with overlapping Whisper output
  when: the second task produces segments whose end timestamps fall before lastTimestamp
  then:
    - duplicate segments are filtered out
    - only novel words (start >= lastTimestamp) are included
```

```mdl
scenario T-4: Open transcript
  given: a Transcript with three Messages in its Feed
  when: op:openTranscript is invoked
  then:
    - content string contains three byline sections
    - each section starts with "## <speaker> · <time>"
```

```mdl
scenario T-5: Summarize transcript
  given: a transcript string and optional notes string
  when: op:summarizeTranscript is invoked
  then:
    - summary is a non-empty Markdown string
    - speaker names appear in bold
    - a tasks section is present if actionable tasks were detected
```

```mdl
scenario T-6: Sentence normalization is pure
  given: an array of raw word-level Messages
  when: op:normalizeSentences is called
  then:
    - output messages contain complete sentences
    - no ECHO writes occur
    - input array is not mutated
```

```mdl
scenario T-7: Toggle recording in UI
  given: TranscriptionArticle is mounted with a Transcript
  when: user clicks the Start Recording toolbar button
  then:
    - recording state becomes true
    - toolbar button label changes to "Stop Recording"
    - microphone capture begins
```

---

## QA

Executable tests. Each step carries a human instruction (`do`) and, where the step maps to an
invocable operation, an agent binding (`invoke`). Report failures by test and step number.
Transcription is enabled by default in every environment (`plugin-defs.tsx` `getDefaults`).

```mdl
test QA-1: Create a transcript and read it back
  desc: |
    The ECHO round-trip that does not require a live microphone or Whisper endpoint — create a
    Transcript, and read its (empty) content back via op:openTranscript.
  actors: agent
  covers: [F-3.1, F-6.1, F-6.2, T-1, T-4]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - no Transcript named "QA Transcript" exists — ABORT rather than deleting one this test did not create
  steps:
    - name: Create the transcript
      do: In the navtree, click + on the space and choose Transcript. Name it "QA Transcript".
      invoke: [op:createTranscript] { name: "QA Transcript", space: $given.space }
      capture: created
      expect: a Transcript named "QA Transcript" now exists, linked to a new Feed
      assert: return !!$created.object && !!$created.object.feed
    - name: Place it in the space
      do: (no separate gesture — the navtree create action places it)
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.addObject { object: $created.object, target: $given.space }
      expect: "QA Transcript" appears as a row in the navtree
    - name: Open it
      do: Click "QA Transcript" in the navtree.
      invoke: [op:openTranscript] { transcript: $created.object }
      expect: the Transcription editor renders (empty, since no messages have been recorded yet)
      assert: return typeof $result.content === 'string'
  after:
    - name: Delete the transcript
      do: Right-click "QA Transcript" in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$created.object], target: $given.space }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```

```mdl
test QA-2: Record, transcribe, and summarize a meeting
  desc: The full audio round-trip — start recording, speak, stop, and summarize what was said.
  actors: both
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-2.2, F-5.1, T-2, T-5, T-7]
  status: blocked
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - transcript: a Transcript open in TranscriptionArticle within that space
    - microphone permission is granted in the browser
    - the Whisper speech-recognition endpoint is reachable
    - recordedContent: a canned transcript string to summarize when the recording steps below are
      not run (they are `blocked` on hardware), so `summarizeTranscript` can still be exercised
      standalone
  steps:
    - name: Start recording
      do: Click the microphone toggle in the toolbar.
      expect: the toolbar button label changes to "Stop Recording" and recording state becomes true
      note: NO `invoke` — microphone capture is a hardware/permission-gated browser action, not an operation.
    - name: Speak a sentence
      do: Say a short sentence aloud, then pause for a couple of seconds.
      expect: a Message with at least one TranscriptSegment of non-empty text is appended to the Feed
      blocked: |
        Cannot run from the debug port: it requires a live microphone, real speech, and a real
        Whisper HTTP call — none of which an automated snippet can produce or fake without
        reimplementing the recording pipeline. Human-only, and unverifiable by an agent even after
        the fact (Rule 9: no invoke, no capability substitute).
    - name: Stop recording
      do: Click the toolbar toggle again.
      expect: capture stops, buffered chunks flush, and the final segment appears in the transcript
      note: NO `invoke` — same as the start-recording step.
    - name: Summarize the transcript
      do: Invoke "Summarize" from the transcript's action menu (or via the assistant skill).
      invoke: [op:summarizeTranscript] { transcript: $given.recordedContent }
      expect: a non-empty Markdown summary is returned with bolded speaker names
      assert: return typeof $result.summary === 'string' && $result.summary.length > 0
      note: |
        `$given.recordedContent` depends on the (blocked) recording steps above having produced
        real text — this step can only run standalone against a canned transcript string, which is
        a legitimate way to exercise op:summarizeTranscript in isolation but does not close the loop
        on the recording pipeline.
  after:
    - name: Delete the transcript
      do: Right-click the Transcript in the navtree and choose Delete.
      invoke: org.dxos.operation.space.removeObjects { objects: [$given.transcript], target: $given.space }
      expect: the row leaves the navtree and its plank closes if it was open
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: The Whistle story transcribes on the device the way Cactus's own demo does, with a low-latency mode, a waveform, a new paragraph after 1.5 s of silence, per-paragraph playback and WAV save, keyword bias, push-to-talk and the engine kept in Cache Storage.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-7]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The Whistle story and the audio tooling are specified in this spec: the pipeline, the pass interval and low-latency mode, the 1.5 s paragraph rule, push-to-talk, keywords, recording retention, playback and WAV save, and fixture-based evals.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-7, F-9]
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Manual tests replay the four agents fixtures through the audio-view Whistle library and report word error rate, words committed in silence and keyword recall: whistle-silence expects no words, whistle-one-two-three expects "one two three", and both echo-query recordings expect "pull up the echo query framework". They are gated on the fixture being present and skipped by CI.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-9.2, F-9.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-4: A compare script runs a recording through bigger models, OpenAI whisper-1 and gpt-4o-transcribe and Cloudflare Workers AI whisper-large-v3-turbo, skipping providers without credentials, and prints the transcripts side by side with word error rate against a reference; Anthropic's API has no audio input, which the script notes rather than calling it.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-9.4]
```

```mdl
decision D-5: A new story extends voice transcription into a home assistant: it uses Cactus's local tool calling, draws a mock home, takes commands such as "turn on the lights", and is optimized for low latency.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8]
```

```mdl
decision D-6: Needle 3 is the local tool-calling model, loaded into the Whistle worker's engine beside Whistle, and the request is answered from the latest pass before the stream's closing pass. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8.1, F-8.3]
  why: The engine holds one text model and one speech model at once and keeps the live stream across an answer, so one worker serves both; the latest pass has already heard the whole request, so waiting for the closing pass only adds its decode time.
  rejected:
    - needle_complete on the raw clip: it transcribes the whole request again after it ends, instead of while it is spoken.
    - A second worker for Needle: twice the engine memory, and the two would still run one after the other on a request.
```

```mdl
decision D-7: Low latency caps the answer at 32 tokens, except for requests joining actions with "and", "then" or "also", which keep 128. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8.4]
  why: Measured in Node on the pinned engine, 32 tokens skips the reasoning line and answers single requests in about 1 s instead of 1.5 s with the same calls; at 32 only the first of two requested calls survives, which the compound rule keeps.
  rejected:
    - 16 tokens: every request came back with no calls.
```

```mdl
decision D-8: The home has five tools, one per action, with enums in the words people say, `all` rooms as the default for lights and blinds, and a warmer/cooler step beside a named temperature. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8.2, F-8.9]
  why: Five or fewer tools all stay in the model's context, where a larger set is retrieved five at a time; separate lock and door-open actions stopped "open the garage" locking it, and the step made "make it warmer" a call instead of a refusal.
```

```mdl
decision D-9: Calls the model withholds are offered for confirmation, never run unasked, and Hands-free ends a request at 0.7 s of trailing silence (0.5 s in Low latency). Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8.5, F-8.6]
  why: Withheld calls are mostly right but unconfirmed (for example "turn on the lights" with no room); a shorter pause answers sooner, and below about half a second a breath inside a request ends it.
```

```mdl
decision D-10: Silence is handled in the worker as audio arrives: the end-of-request marker goes into the audio queue exactly where the pause ends, passes pause after 0.15 s of silence, and streams that hear nothing are ended after 1 s. Fills in [D-5].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-8.3, F-8.5, F-8.10]
  why: Measured in Chromium with spoken commands, ending requests from the main thread on the live recording merged consecutive commands whenever passes fell behind, and re-decoding the silence between commands added about a second to each answer; with the worker handling it, every command split correctly and single commands answered in 0.95 to 1.8 s after the pause, against about 1 s of model time.
  rejected:
    - Ending requests on the main thread from each result: results arrive a pass late, so the silence measured is not the silence the pass heard.
```

```mdl
decision D-11: In the fixture evals, accurate mode (1 s passes) must stay at or under 50% word error rate and commit no words during silence, low-latency mode must commit words and only logs its error rate, keyword recall is logged rather than asserted, and the silence recording is an expected failure while Whistle still commits "Thank you." over room tone. Digits score as number words. Fills in [D-3].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-9.3]
  why: The recordings are few and short, so tight bounds would fail on one word; the expected failure turns into a failing test once Whistle stops inventing words over silence, which is the signal to make it a plain test. Whistle writes "1. 2. 3." for "one two three", which is correct and scored 100% wrong before.
```

```mdl
decision D-12: Whistle committing "Thank you." over the silence recording is fixed in this change, not left as an expected failure.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-7.10, F-9.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-13: Silence is never decoded: a stream opens only once 0.15 s of audio is louder than both the noise-floor threshold and -35 dBFS, with 0.5 s of pre-roll, in the worker and in the replay the evals use; whistle-silence becomes a plain test. Fills in [D-12]. Supersedes the expected failure in [D-11].
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-7.10, F-9.3]
  supersedes: D-11
  why: Whistle alone, and Cloudflare's whisper-large-v3-turbo too, transcribe the fixture's room tone as "Thank you.", so no model setting removes it; its 50 ms bars peak at -37 dBFS while every speech fixture has 27 or more bars above -35, and the speech fixtures transcribe the same with the gate as without it.
  rejected:
    - The noise-floor threshold alone: the room tone sits 30 dB above its own floor, so it counts as sound.
    - Dropping "Thank you." from transcripts: it is a real phrase, and other inventions would remain.
```

```mdl
decision D-14: The rest of [D-11] stands: accurate mode at or under 50% word error rate with no words committed in silence, low-latency mode committing words with its error rate logged, keyword recall logged, and digits scored as number words.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-9.3]
```

```mdl
decision D-15: The Whistle hook, capture, protocol and worker move from the story folder to `src/whistle`, exported as `@dxos/plugin-transcription/Whistle`, so other plugins can take spoken input; the stories import it from there.
  date: 2026-10-23
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-7]
  why: Code Graph's command bar asked for the microphone and Whistle, and the stories held the only copy.
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext type
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0
  desc: A named data structure with typed fields and optional literals.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    fields?: FieldMap        # name[?]: TypeExpr  (# inline comment)
    literals?: UnionList     # a | b | c
    extends?: TypeRef[]
```

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap            # external inputs (immutable inside component)
    state?: FieldMap            # internal reactive state
    slots?: FieldMap            # named ReactNode injection points
    actions?: ActionMap         # methods the component exposes or handles
    emits?: EventMap            # events the component raises to its parent
    layout?: CodeBlock          # ASCII sketch of visual structure (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap            # named input parameters
    output?: TypeExpr           # return type
    errors?: ErrorMap           # name: Prose  (when this error occurs)
    effects?: EffectList        # echo:read | echo:write | http | fs | ...
    requires?: ServiceList      # injected service dependencies
    note?: Prose                # implementation guidance (non-normative)
```
